"""
@ingroup PATTERN_API
@brief Add sewing between sub-segments of two pattern outline lines (pattern A line <-> pattern B line).
Unlike AddSeamlinePairGroup, which always sews the whole line, each side here sews only the
portion of its line between the given ratios, so a seam can cover part of an edge.
The resulting stitch is identical to a manually created one and simulates the same way.
@return Marvelous::SeamlinePairGroupResult - SEAMLINE_PAIR_SUCCESS (0) on success, a negative code on failure.
Test against SEAMLINE_PAIR_SUCCESS rather than for truthiness, because 0 is falsy in Python.
@param _patternAIndex : A pattern index
@param _lineAIndex : The index of the line that belongs to the A pattern.
@param _startRatioA : Where the seam starts along the A line, normalized to the line length. 0.0 is the line start, 1.0 the line end.
@param _endRatioA : Where the seam ends along the A line. Must be strictly greater than _startRatioA.
@param _directionA : The direction of the stitching, true : forward, false : backward
@param _patternBIndex : B pattern index
@param _lineBIndex : The index of the line that belongs to the B pattern.
@param _startRatioB : Where the seam starts along the B line, normalized to the line length.
@param _endRatioB : Where the seam ends along the B line. Must be strictly greater than _startRatioB.
@param _directionB : The direction of the stitching, true : forward, false : backward
@remark Ratios are used verbatim; notch snapping is not applied. Call from the thread that owns the
scene, as with the other pattern-editing APIs.
@remark This call reports only a status code. To act on the new seam afterwards, diff
GetSeamlinePairGroupListInPattern(_patternAIndex) across the call to get its index.
"""

